#. translators: %s: the warning code.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:59
#, php-format
msgid "Unknown warning (%s)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:120
msgid "This kind of data is not supported, so it is skipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:124
msgid "An unexpected error occurred while processing this item, so it is skipped. The error is recorded in the Logs tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:125
msgid "Check the error in the Logs tab and fix its cause (usually the item’s data or another plugin), then run again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:129
msgid "This item was imported from the platform, so it is not exported back to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:133
msgid "This item was created in WooCommerce and exported to the platform, so importing does not overwrite it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:139
msgid "WooCommerce does not treat entered prices as including tax, while the platform’s prices include tax and are imported as they are. This is a store-wide setting; only one product per batch is flagged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:140
msgid "If WooCommerce calculates tax, set “Prices entered with tax” to “Yes, I will enter prices inclusive of tax” in WooCommerce > Settings > Tax. Otherwise tax is added on top at checkout. If tax calculation is turned off, no change is needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:145
msgid "The store currency is not Japanese yen. The order is imported in the store currency with the platform’s yen amounts unchanged (for example, ¥1,000 becomes 1,000 in the store currency)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:146
msgid "Set the store currency to Japanese yen in WooCommerce > Settings > General before importing orders. Orders that were already imported keep their currency."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:150
msgid "The currency is not Japanese yen, so the item is not exported (the platform would treat the amounts as yen)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a currency code, such as USD.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:153
#, php-format
msgid "The currency %s is not Japanese yen, so the item is not exported (the platform would treat the amounts as yen)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:157
msgid "Prices in WooCommerce are entered without tax, so they are exported with tax added at the rate for the store’s address. Only the first product in each batch is flagged; the others are converted the same way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:161
msgid "The sale price is exported, but the sale’s end date cannot be sent, so the platform keeps the sale price after the sale ends in WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:162
msgid "After the sale ends, export the product again or change the price on the platform."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:164
#, php-format
msgid "The sale price of variation %s is exported, but the sale’s end date cannot be sent, so the platform keeps the sale price after the sale ends in WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:168
msgid "The price cannot be converted to a price including tax: the tax class has tax rates, but none of them applies to the store’s address. The product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:169
msgid "Add a tax rate that applies to the store’s address (or to all locations) to the tax class in WooCommerce > Settings > Tax, or correct the store address."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:171
#, php-format
msgid "The price of variation %s cannot be converted to a price including tax: its tax class has tax rates, but none of them applies to the store’s address. The product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:175
msgid "The tax class given by the platform does not exist in WooCommerce, so the item uses the standard tax class."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:176
msgid "Create the tax class in WooCommerce > Settings > Tax and set it on the item. If tax calculation is turned off in WooCommerce > Settings > General, no change is needed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the slug of a tax class.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:178
#, php-format
msgid "The tax class “%s” given by the platform does not exist in WooCommerce, so the item uses the standard tax class."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:182
msgid "The item is put in a tax class that has no tax rates (for a reduced-rate item, the default reduced rate class), so WooCommerce charges no tax on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:183
msgid "If WooCommerce calculates tax, add the correct Japanese tax rate to that tax class in WooCommerce > Settings > Tax (for the reduced rate class, 8%); you do not need to import again. If tax calculation is turned off in WooCommerce > Settings > General, no change is needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:187
msgid "WooCommerce has no tax class with a Japanese rate (8%) for reduced-rate items, so the item uses the standard tax class."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:188
msgid "In WooCommerce > Settings > Tax (shown when tax calculation is turned on in WooCommerce > Settings > General), give a tax class for the reduced rate (such as “Reduced rate”) a Japanese rate of 8%. Then import again: products are corrected, but orders that were already imported keep the standard tax class."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:192
msgid "The product’s tax class has no Japanese tax rate of 10% (standard) or 8% (reduced), so the product is not exported (it would be sold with the wrong tax)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:193
msgid "Change the product’s tax class to the standard or reduced rate, or give the tax class a Japanese tax rate: 10% (standard) or 8% (reduced). (The tax settings and the product’s tax fields are shown only when tax calculation is turned on in WooCommerce > Settings > General.)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the name of a tax class. Write a literal percent sign as %%.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:195
#, php-format
msgid "The tax class “%s” has no Japanese tax rate of 10%% (standard) or 8%% (reduced), so the product is not exported (it would be sold with the wrong tax)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:199
msgid "The tax class of a published variation has no Japanese tax rate of 10% (standard) or 8% (reduced), so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:200
msgid "Change the variation’s tax class (or the product’s, if the variation uses the same as its parent) to the standard or reduced rate, or give the tax class a Japanese tax rate: 10% (standard) or 8% (reduced). (The tax settings and the product’s tax fields are shown only when tax calculation is turned on in WooCommerce > Settings > General.)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation. Write a literal percent sign as %%.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:202
#, php-format
msgid "The tax class of variation %s has no Japanese tax rate of 10%% (standard) or 8%% (reduced), so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:206
msgid "The product’s tax status is “Shipping only” or “None”, which the platform cannot represent, so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:207
msgid "If the product is taxed, set its tax status to “Taxable”. Otherwise, add the product on the platform by hand. (The tax settings and the product’s tax fields are shown only when tax calculation is turned on in WooCommerce > Settings > General.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:211
msgid "The product’s prices cannot be converted to the platform’s prices because the platform’s tax settings cannot be used, so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:212
msgid "Check the tax settings on the platform (prices including or excluding tax, the standard and reduced rates, and rounding), then export again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:218
msgid "The SKU is already used by another product in WooCommerce, so the item is imported without a SKU."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:219
msgid "Make the SKU unique (change it on the platform, or change or delete the WooCommerce product that uses it), then enter the SKU on the imported item."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: a SKU.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:221
#, php-format
msgid "The SKU “%s” is already used by another product in WooCommerce, so the item is imported without a SKU."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:226
msgid "The product’s price from the platform is not a number or is negative, so the price is not set. A new product cannot be bought until it has a price; an existing product keeps its previous price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:227
msgid "Correct the price on the platform and import again, or set the price in WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the price value received from the platform.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:229
#, php-format
msgid "The product’s price from the platform (%s) is not a number or is negative, so the price is not set. A new product cannot be bought until it has a price; an existing product keeps its previous price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:233
msgid "The product has no valid price, or its price cannot be converted to a price including tax, so it is not exported. A simple product needs a regular price; a variable product needs at least one enabled variation with a price that is shown in the store."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:234
msgid "Set a regular price. For a variable product, enable a variation with a price; if “Hide out of stock items” is on, at least one variation must be in stock. If the product also has a warning that its price cannot be converted to a price including tax, fix the tax rate as that warning describes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:238
msgid "The sale price from the platform is not valid (it must be more than 0 and lower than the regular price), so the product is imported without a sale."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:239
msgid "Correct the sale price on the platform, then import again."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the sale price value received from the platform.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:241
#, php-format
msgid "The sale price from the platform (%s) is not valid (it must be more than 0 and lower than the regular price), so the product is imported without a sale."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:245
msgid "An image could not be downloaded from the platform, so it is not added. The item’s other images are added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:246
msgid "Check that the image can be opened from your server, then add it to the item in WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the URL of an image.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:248
#, php-format
msgid "The image %s could not be downloaded from the platform, so it is not added. The item’s other images are added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:252
msgid "An attribute has the same name as one of the product’s variation options, so the attribute is not imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:253
msgid "Rename the attribute on the platform, then import again."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the name of an attribute.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:255
#, php-format
msgid "The attribute “%s” has the same name as one of the product’s variation options, so it is not imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:259
msgid "A variation that was imported earlier no longer exists on the platform, so it is deleted from WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:262
#, php-format
msgid "The variation %s no longer exists on the platform, so it is deleted from WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:267
msgid "A variation’s price from the platform is not a number or is negative, so the variation is not created or updated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:268
msgid "Correct the variation’s price on the platform, then import again."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:270
#, php-format
msgid "The price of variation %s from the platform is not a number or is negative, so the variation is not created or updated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:274
msgid "A variation has no valid regular price, or its price cannot be converted to a price including tax, so it is left out of the export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:275
msgid "Set a regular price on the variation, then export again. If its price cannot be converted to a price including tax, the whole product is not exported; fix the tax rate as that warning describes. A variation that was exported before stays on the platform; hide it there if needed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:277
#, php-format
msgid "Variation %s has no valid regular price, or its price cannot be converted to a price including tax, so it is left out of the export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:281
msgid "Some variations from the platform could not be read, so variations that no longer exist on the platform are not deleted for this product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:282
msgid "Correct the variations on the platform (usually their prices), then import again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:286
msgid "WooCommerce could not save a variation, so it is not created. The product and its other variations are imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:287
msgid "Check the PHP error log for the cause."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:289
#, php-format
msgid "WooCommerce could not save the variation %s, so it is not created. The product and its other variations are imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:293
msgid "WooCommerce could not save the product, so it is not imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:294
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:733
msgid "Check the PHP error log for the cause, then import again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:298
msgid "A category of the product is not mapped to a category on the platform, so the product is exported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:299
msgid "Map the category in the Mappings tab, then export again."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a product category.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:301
#, php-format
msgid "The category (ID %s) is not mapped to a category on the platform, so the product is exported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:305
msgid "A variation is not enabled, so it is left out of the export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:306
msgid "If the variation should be sold, enable it and export again. A variation that was exported before stays on the platform; hide it there if needed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:308
#, php-format
msgid "Variation %s is not enabled, so it is left out of the export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:312
msgid "The product uses three or more attributes for variations, but the platform supports at most two, so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:313
msgid "Use at most two attributes for variations (combine attributes, or turn off “Used for variations” on the others)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:317
msgid "None of the product’s variations can be exported (they are not enabled or have no valid price, or the product has no variations), so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:318
msgid "Enable at least one variation with a valid price. The other warnings for this product show why each variation was left out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:322
msgid "A variation uses “Any” for an attribute, which the platform cannot represent, so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:323
msgid "Replace the “Any” variation with one variation for each value of the attribute."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the WooCommerce ID of a variation.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:325
#, php-format
msgid "Variation %s uses “Any” for an attribute, which the platform cannot represent, so the product is not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:329
msgid "The variations’ stock settings are mixed: some manage stock and others do not, or variations that do not manage stock differ in stock status (in stock and out of stock). A platform that manages stock per product cannot represent this, so the product and its stock are not exported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:330
msgid "Turn on stock management for all variations, or turn it off for all variations and give them all the same stock status (all in stock or all out of stock)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:334
msgid "A variation’s stock is managed by its parent product, and the platform cannot share stock between variations, so the variation is exported as out of stock."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:335
msgid "Turn on “Manage stock” for each variation and give it its own quantity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:341
msgid "The parent category is not found in WooCommerce, so the category is placed at the top level for now. It is moved under its parent when it is imported again after the parent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:342
msgid "Import categories; parent categories are imported first. If this remains after an import, check why the parent category was not imported."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a category.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:344
#, php-format
msgid "The parent category %s is not found in WooCommerce, so the category is placed at the top level for now. It is moved under its parent when it is imported again after the parent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:348
msgid "A category of the product is not found in WooCommerce, so the product is imported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:349
msgid "Import categories before products (a full import does this). If this remains, the category is not imported, for example because it is hidden on the platform or its name conflicts with an existing category."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a category.
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:351
#, php-format
msgid "The product’s category %s is not found in WooCommerce, so the product is imported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:355
msgid "A tag (group) of the product is not found in WooCommerce, so the product is imported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:356
msgid "Import tags before products (a full import does this). If this remains, the tag is not imported, for example because it is not public on the platform or its name conflicts with an existing tag."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the platform's ID of a tag (group).
#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:358
#, php-format
msgid "The product’s tag (group) %s is not found in WooCommerce, so the product is imported without it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Woo/WarningCatalog.php:362
msgid "A category or tag with the same name under the same parent was imported from this platform before, so it is reused."
